    flynnContext: "IQ 52 today corresponds to approximately IQ 40–43 on 1950 norms. A person with this raw cognitive ability in 1950 would likely have lived most of their adult life in a state institution or with family without access to education, employment, or community participation. The dramatic improvement in functional outcomes for today's individuals at this score reflects the cumulative impact of Flynn Effect biological gains, IDEA legislation, and disability rights movements that are not captured in the IQ number itself.",
