    flynnContext: "Calibrated to 1950 norms, IQ 53 corresponds to approximately IQ 41–44. A person with this raw cognitive ability in 1950 would likely have spent most of their adult life in a state institution or sheltered home without access to education, employment, or community participation. The dramatic improvement in functional outcomes for today's individuals at this score reflects the cumulative impact of Flynn Effect biological gains, IDEA legislation, and disability rights movements — changes that are not visible in the IQ number itself.",
