    flynnContext: "IQ 97 today corresponds to approximately IQ 85–88 on 1950 norms. The 3-point gap from the mean of 100 is statistically negligible and functionally meaningless for virtually all daily-life and occupational purposes. The Flynn Effect has moved the raw cognitive ability associated with IQ 97 substantially upward across generations, reflecting genuine improvements in human cognitive development. Today's person at IQ 97 operates with full confidence across all mainstream educational and professional environments.",
