    flynnContext: "IQ 108 today corresponds to approximately IQ 96–99 on 1950 norms. The 8-point advantage over the mean is beginning to represent a meaningful systematic cognitive advantage in the most demanding academic and professional contexts. The Flynn Effect has raised raw cognitive ability at this level substantially across generations. Today's person at IQ 108 possesses greater actual cognitive capacity than their 1950 equivalent, reflecting genuine generational improvements driven by better nutrition, healthcare, and enriched educational environments.",
